<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis de Bourmont</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1773–1846</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Louis-Auguste-Victor de Ghaisne de Bourmont</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis de Bourmont (1773–1846) was a French general and royalist who had fought in the Vendée revolt before serving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>, whom he deserted on the eve of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-waterloo">Waterloo</a>. As minister of war under Charles X, he led the expedition that captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a> in July 1830 and was made a marshal of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. After the July Revolution he refused to serve <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-philippe-i">Louis-Philippe</a> and went into exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-de-bourmont.jpg" alt="Louis de Bourmont" width="320" height="510" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marechal-de-bourmont.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
